# claude-seat-1: task 1790632438 ("A pot won because everybody folded must not show the winner's hole cards to the table")

Closes: 1790632438 (done)

Executor handover: the first executor wrote and committed the fix (d6a6910) and started the
full fast gate, then died (session spend limit) before writing this file. A second executor
verified what was on disk, re-ran every cheap gate, reconstructed the red evidence for the
view predicate, and integrated. Nothing was changed on the branch after d6a6910.

## What landed (branch claude/seat-1, on top of main 88a4f75; `git merge main` was a no-op)

- d6a6910 fix: a pot won because everybody folded no longer shows the winner's cards to the table (E-107, review gap 3; task 1790632438)
  - src/table_canister/src/lib.rs: `TableState.last_hand_went_to_showdown: Option<bool>`, `#[serde(default)]`, `opt bool` on the wire (FINDING 14's rule: `TableState` sits inside `opt TableState`, so a bare addition would wipe the table on upgrade); `None` reads as "not a showdown", the hiding direction. Written by `finish_hand(state, now, went_to_showdown)`, the one place that writes `HandComplete`: `true` from `determine_winners`, `false` from `end_hand_single_winner` and `settle_unmovable_hand` (the same bool those callers already hand `record_hand_to_history`).
  - `get_table_view` body extracted to `pub fn build_table_view(state, caller, now)` (host-testable from any principal). Reveal predicate is now `phase == Showdown || (phase == HandComplete && last_hand_went_to_showdown())`; a fold-out winner's cards are `None` for every other caller, seated or stranger, until the next deal.
  - `show_cards` body extracted to `pub fn record_voluntary_show(state, caller)`; a voluntary show is accepted only at `Showdown` or `HandComplete`, folded or not. Before, only an UNFOLDED seat was refused mid-hand, so a folded seat could turn its cards up while others were still playing.
  - src/table_canister/table_canister.did: `TableState` gains `last_hand_went_to_showdown : opt bool` (the `get_table_state` reply). `TableView` is unchanged. src/declarations/table_{1,2,3}/ regenerated with `check-declarations-js.sh --write`.
  - src/table_canister/tests/betting_rules.rs section 7: four tests over the real deal and `build_table_view` from every seat's point of view and a stranger's at every phase (fold-out hides the winner; showdown still reveals every unfolded hand and keeps the mucked one hidden; mid-hand show refused, post-hand show reveals; a table restored without the flag at `HandComplete` hides everything). One-line struct-literal touches in coherence_regressions.rs, hand_membership.rs, money_safety.rs and the in-crate test fixtures.
  - src/cleardeck_frontend/src/lib/showdown.js (new) + showdown.test.js (new): `handsAreFaceUp(phaseKey, lastWinners)` is true at `Showdown`, and at `HandComplete` only if some winner record carries `cards`, which `push_winner` attaches only at a showdown. PokerTable.svelte's `isShowdown` reads it; own cards and the live seat's card backs stay up through the `HandComplete` pause via `isHandComplete`; after a fold-out the live seat is the winner record's seat. No new `TableView` field was needed.
  - docs/DEFECTS.md: E-107 (medium, FIXED, task 1790632438) register row and write-up with the red output. docs/CODEBASE-REVIEW-2026-09-28.md gap 3 now points at E-107.
  - No settlement arithmetic changed; no balance code touched; no check weakened.

